Lekmap v6.0.6 (since v6.0.5)
============================

Start placement (Fractal Pangaea)
---------------------------------
- Inland seas now count for the start distance rules: majors stay 4+ tiles from inland-sea water and
  city states are never 1-2 tiles from it. Inland seas still do not make a start coastal.
- Coastal capitals no longer have water or mountains in the center-facing half of their first two rings:
  those tiles become flat land or hills matching the neighbours. Coastal start spots whose only ocean
  contact faces the center are rejected.

Islands
-------
- Sea stacks (splintered cliffs tiny) are less regular: most rows push 1-2 stacks one tile further out;
  the first stack stays one water tile off the coast.

Resources (both maps)
---------------------
- No resources on natural wonder tiles; wonders skip tiles that already hold a resource.
- Luxury diversity: a city state shares its luxury type with at most 1 of its 5 nearest city states.
  A random luxury is not placed where 2+ of the 6 nearest luxuries are the same type (another type is
  swapped in, or the tile is skipped). Regional and start luxuries are unchanged.
- Amber only comes in clusters: when amber is a random luxury, 1-3 locations near salt water get 1-3
  ambers each, usually under forest or jungle. Amber is never a regional, city state or start luxury.
